# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile copies the build machine's
# working tree into the image — on top of the `npm ci` that ran just before it.
# Three separate problems, all fixed by excluding the entries below:
#
#   1. node_modules built on the host overwrite the ones npm ci installed.
#      The host is glibc and the image is node:26-alpine (musl), so any native
#      module lands in the image compiled for the wrong libc.
#   2. .env is baked into an image layer — JWT secret, Mongo root password,
#      Redis password, LiveKit secret. Anyone who can pull the image has them.
#      Config is supplied at runtime via env_file, so it must not be in here.
#   3. 556MB of node_modules plus .git for no reason.

node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Secrets — supplied at runtime, never baked into an image layer.
#   .env         -> docker-compose `env_file`
#   credentials/ -> docker-compose bind mount at /app/credentials:ro
#
# The credentials mount is not optional: src/services/fcmService.js requires
# firebase-service-account.json at module load, so a container without it does
# not start. If you run this image outside the compose file, mount the
# directory (or drop the exclusion) or it will exit on boot.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials/
*-service-account.json
serviceAccountKey.json

# VCS and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local runtime state
uploads/
logs/
*.log
pids/
*.pid

# Dev-only tooling
load-test/
.claude/

# Docs and local compose config
*.md
docker-compose.yml
observability/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
deploy.sh
